WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.430
In Cairo, a browser asks for Arabic,

2
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.990
and your page still shows
its count in English.

3
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:09.570
Its plural comes from a
check for n equals one,

4
00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.650
and Arabic needs different
sentences for two, three and eleven.

5
00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:18.490
General Translation handles plurals
in React with the Plural component.

6
00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:26.080
Run npx gt init, sign in, then give
Plural the count and sentences for zero,

7
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.030
for one and for more.

8
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:31.770
Wrap it in a T component,
with the count inside Num.

9
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:36.800
Run npx gt translate, and it
writes the sentences that Spanish,

10
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.670
Japanese and Arabic need.

11
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:42.850
In Cairo, Plural now picks
the Arabic sentence for two,

12
00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.910
for three and for eleven.
